</ElicitationsGroup>Á
well its exiting with code 100Exit code 100 almost always happens if you are using **Linux** or **Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL)**. 

This error happens because Playwright is trying to use your system's package manager (`apt`) to install those background libraries, but your system's package list is outdated or it doesn't have the necessary admin permissions to run the installation.

Here is the exact sequence to fix this:

<Sequence>
  <Step title="Update your system's package list">
    Run this command to refresh the list of available software. It will likely ask for your computer's password.
    ```bash
    sudo apt-get update
    ```
  </Step>

  <Step title="Install the dependencies as an admin">
    Force Playwright to install the dependencies with `sudo` (admin rights) so it doesn't get blocked.
    ```bash
    sudo npx playwright install-deps
    ```
  </Step>

  <Step title="Install the Playwright browsers">
    Now that the background libraries are installed, run the standard browser installation:
    ```bash
    npx playwright install
    ```
  </Step>
</Sequence>

Once those finish, try running your test again with `npx playwright test`. 

