how to  update node ÉThe fastest way to update Node.js depends on your operating system. 

**For Windows or macOS (The Easiest Method)**
1. Go to the official [Node.js website](https://nodejs.org/).
2. Download the **LTS (Long Term Support)** installer.
3. Run the installer and click through the prompts. It will automatically overwrite your existing Node.js version and update `npm` along with it.

**For Linux, macOS, or WSL (Using the Terminal)**
You can update Node directly from your command line using a package called `n`. Run these commands one by one:
1. Clean your current npm cache: 
   ```bash
   sudo npm cache clean -f
   ```
2. Install the `n` version manager globally: 
   ```bash
   sudo npm install -g n
   ```
3. Upgrade Node to the latest LTS version: 
   ```bash
   sudo n lts
   ```

**For Windows (Using PowerShell)**
If you are on Windows 10 or 11 and prefer the command line, open PowerShell and use the built-in package manager:
```powershell
winget upgrade OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS
```

After using any of these methods, **completely close your terminal or command prompt and open a new one**. Verify the update was successful by typing:
```bash
node -v
```

<ElicitationsGroup message="What would you like to do next?">
  <Elicitation label="Retry Playwright install" query="Now that Node is updated, how do I retry the Playwright installation?"/>
  <Elicitation label="Node didn't update" query="I ran the steps, but 'node -v' still shows the old version."/>
</ElicitationsGroup>­
