Ïcurl: (56) Recv failure: Connection reset by peer

xz: (stdin): Unexpected end of input
tar: Unexpected EOF in archive
tar: Unexpected EOF in archive
tar: Error is not recoverable: exiting now
 what is this µ
This is a network connection error. Your internet connection dropped, or the server disconnected you right in the middle of downloading the Node.js update. 

Because the download was interrupted, the downloaded archive file was incomplete, which is why the extraction tools (`tar` and `xz`) threw an "Unexpected end of input" error when trying to open it.

Here is how to fix it:

<Sequence>
  <Step title="Retry the command">
    Network hiccups are often temporary. Simply run the command one more time:
    ```bash
    sudo n lts
    ```
  </Step>

  <Step title="Clear the corrupted file (If it fails again)">
    If it fails a second time, the incomplete file might be stuck in the cache. Remove it by running:
    ```bash
    sudo n rm lts
    ```
    Then try running `sudo n lts` again.
  </Step>
</Sequence>

If your network consistently blocks this download, we can use the official Ubuntu/Debian package manager (`apt`) instead of `n` to get Node.js.

