;well i am student as i have not even worked as a developer »Being a student without professional developer experience is completely normalâ€”in fact, it is the standard starting point for entry-level SDET and QA automation roles. 

Hiring managers recruiting for entry-level SDETs, QA interns, or associate engineers do not expect years of enterprise software building. What they actually evaluate is your grasp of programming fundamentals, your understanding of how the web works, and your ability to write clean, automated tests.

**Why Being a Student Is Actually an Advantage**

* **Modern Tech Stack:** Many working QA engineers are still stuck using legacy tools like Selenium with Java. Learning Playwright with JavaScript/TypeScript puts you directly on the modern stack companies are actively migrating toward.
* **Low Competition in QA Automation:** Thousands of CS students blindly compete for standard Software Engineering (SWE) internships, while far fewer actively prepare for SDET roles. Demonstrating genuine Playwright skills makes your application immediately stand out.
* **Your Portfolio Acts as Experience:** For entry-level roles, a public GitHub repository with a clean Playwright framework, Page Object Model architecture, and automated CI/CD runs serves as your "proof of work" in place of a past job.

**How to Target Your Strategy as a Student**

* **Target Specific Entry Titles:** Search for **QA Engineering Intern**, **Junior SDET**, **Associate QA Automation Engineer**, or **Graduate Test Engineer**.
* **Build Practical Projects:** Employers care far more about code you've published than passive course completion certificates. One solid test suite on GitHub beats five certificates on LinkedIn.
* **Master the "Breaker" Mindset:** Developers write code to make features work; SDETs write code to find edge cases, failure points, and performance bottlenecks. Developing this mindset early is what wins interviews.

You do not need to work as a developer first to become an SDET. By taking this step-by-step approach to building a real automation framework, you are creating the exact portfolio needed to land a job directly out of school.

